section: compiler
synopsis: Fix the RISC-V NCG sign-extending the result of atomic reads of subword values
issues: #28130
mrs: !16997

description: {
  Atomic reads of 8-, 16-, and 32-bit values used a signed load (``LDR``),
  which left the upper bits sign-extended. This violated the zero-extended
  subword invariant maintained by the RISC-V NCG, so for example an atomic
  read of a byte holding ``0xff`` produced ``-1`` instead of ``255``.

  The reads now use ``LDRU``, which maps to ``lbu``, ``lhu``, ``lwu``, or
  ``ld`` depending on the width.
}
